<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — NCare (Sylvana Care)"
  description="Privacy policy for the NCare mobile application, published by Sylvana Care. Treatment management, medication reminders, appointments and health tracking. nFADP and GDPR compliance."
  canonicalPath="/en/privacy-ncare"
  pageTitle="Privacy Policy — NCare"
  pageSubtitle="Mobile app for treatment management and health tracking"
  effectiveDate="August 12, 2026"
>
  <h2>1. App and publisher identification</h2>
  <p>
    This privacy policy applies to the <strong>NCare</strong> mobile application
    (Google Play ID: <strong>com.sylvanacare.pills</strong>), hereinafter “the App”.
  </p>
  <p>The App is published by:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Publisher (Google Play Developer):</strong> Sylvana Care</li>
    <li><strong>Application:</strong> NCare</li>
    <li><strong>Package ID:</strong> com.sylvanacare.pills</li>
    <li><strong>Data protection contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:dr.aneyret@hin.ch">dr.aneyret@hin.ch</a></li>
    <li><strong>Jurisdiction:</strong> Switzerland</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="legal-note">
    This document, together with the disclosures shown inside the App, describes how
    <strong>Sylvana Care</strong> accesses, collects, uses, shares and protects your data
    within the <strong>NCare</strong> App.
  </div>

  <h2>2. Legal framework</h2>
  <p>
    We process your data in accordance with the
    <em>Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (nFADP)</em> and the
    <em>General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)</em> of the European Union.
    As NCare is a health application, your medical data is treated as
    <strong>sensitive data</strong> with a reinforced level of protection.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Data we collect</h2>

  <h3>3.1 Account and identity</h3>
  <p>To create and secure your account via Firebase Authentication, we collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Email address and, where applicable, password (stored encrypted by Firebase)</li>
    <li>First and last name</li>
    <li>Phone number (if you provide it)</li>
    <li>Third-party sign-in identifiers when you use <strong>Google Sign-In</strong> or <strong>Sign in with Apple</strong></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3.2 Health data (sensitive)</h3>
  <p>At the core of the App, you can enter and view:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your medications, prescriptions, dosages and schedules</li>
    <li>Your reminders and medication intake times</li>
    <li>Your medical appointments</li>
    <li>Your biomarkers, health scores, goals and targets</li>
    <li>Your dietetics information and exercise programs</li>
    <li>Any personal notes you add to these items</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3.3 AI assistant (chatbot)</h3>
  <p>
    When you use the AI assistant, the content of your messages is sent to our service to
    generate a response. Please avoid entering information you do not wish to have processed.
  </p>

  <h3>3.4 Technical and diagnostic data</h3>
  <p>To ensure the App's stability and security, we collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Crash and performance reports via <strong>Firebase Crashlytics</strong></li>
    <li>Device model, operating system and App version</li>
    <li>Technical logs of exchanges with our server (for debugging purposes)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3.5 Push notifications</h3>
  <p>
    A notification identifier (<strong>Firebase Cloud Messaging</strong> token) is associated
    with your device to send you treatment reminders and important messages.
  </p>

  <h3>3.6 Camera and barcode scanning</h3>
  <p>
    The App may use the camera to scan a medication barcode (GS1 standard) to make data entry
    easier. Camera images are processed to read the code and are not retained for this purpose.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Device permissions</h2>
  <p>The App requests certain permissions, only for the related features:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Camera</strong>: scanning medication barcodes</li>
    <li><strong>Microphone / audio</strong>: video playback and interactive features</li>
    <li><strong>Notifications & exact alarms</strong>: medication reminders at the scheduled time</li>
    <li><strong>Storage / files</strong>: viewing and sharing resources and documents</li>
    <li><strong>Run at boot</strong>: rescheduling reminders after a device restart</li>
    <li><strong>Internet</strong>: synchronization with our servers</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Why we use your data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide the App's features: reminders, treatment tracking, appointments, health monitoring</li>
    <li>Authenticate you and secure access to your account</li>
    <li>Send you the reminder notifications you have configured</li>
    <li>Ensure proper operation, fix bugs and improve the App</li>
    <li>Respond to your support requests</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Legal basis for processing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Performance of the service</strong>: processing necessary to provide the features you request</li>
    <li><strong>Consent</strong>: for sensitive health data and notifications, withdrawable at any time</li>
    <li><strong>Legitimate interest</strong>: security, fraud prevention and improvement of the App</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Data sharing</h2>
  <p>
    Your data is <strong>never sold</strong> or used for advertising purposes.
    It may only be processed by technical providers acting on our behalf:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Firebase</strong> (Authentication, Cloud Messaging, Crashlytics) — authentication, notifications and diagnostics infrastructure</li>
    <li>Our <strong>application server (NCare API)</strong>, which hosts your health data</li>
    <li>The <strong>AI assistant</strong> provider, for conversation content only</li>
    <li><strong>Competent authorities</strong>, only where required by law (e.g. a court order)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Some providers (notably Google Firebase) may process data outside Switzerland or the
    European Union. Such transfers are governed by appropriate safeguards (standard contractual
    clauses, adequacy decisions) in accordance with the nFADP and the GDPR.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Data retention</h2>
  <p>
    Your data is retained for as long as your account is active. If you delete your account,
    your personal and health data is deleted or anonymized within a reasonable timeframe, unless
    a legal retention obligation applies. Diagnostic reports are kept for a limited period.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Security</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Authentication tokens are stored encrypted on the device (secure storage)</li>
    <li>Data cached locally is encrypted (AES-256)</li>
    <li>Exchanges with our servers are protected by HTTPS/TLS</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>11. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the nFADP and the GDPR, you have the following rights:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Right of access</strong> to your data</li>
    <li><strong>Right to rectification</strong> of inaccurate data</li>
    <li><strong>Right to erasure</strong> (right to be forgotten)</li>
    <li><strong>Right to data portability</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Right to object</strong> and to restrict processing</li>
    <li><strong>Right to withdraw consent</strong> at any time</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise these rights, contact us at
    <a href="mailto:dr.aneyret@hin.ch">dr.aneyret@hin.ch</a>. We respond within a maximum of 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Deleting your account and data</h2>
  <p>You can request deletion of your account and associated data:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>From within the App, via your profile options (account deletion)</li>
    <li>Or by emailing <a href="mailto:dr.aneyret@hin.ch">dr.aneyret@hin.ch</a> with the subject “Account deletion”</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="legal-note">
    Deleting your account results in the erasure of your personal and health data, subject to any
    applicable legal retention obligations.
  </div>

  <h2>13. Children</h2>
  <p>
    NCare is not intended for children under 16. We do not knowingly collect data about minors
    without the consent of a holder of parental authority.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    This policy may change to comply with legal requirements or reflect updates to the App.
    The online version always prevails; the effective date at the top of this page indicates the
    latest update.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For any question about your data or this policy, contact the publisher
    <strong>Sylvana Care</strong>:
    <a href="mailto:dr.aneyret@hin.ch">dr.aneyret@hin.ch</a>.
  </p>

  <a href="/en/" class="legal-back">← Back to homepage</a>
</LegalLayout>
